{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_81","type":"agent_message","text":"The token-centric RoPE mapping is bit-identical and modestly faster, especially for large batches. One remaining high-value target is the AdaLN projection: half of its output is unused, but naïvely narrowing it changes the BLAS reduction algorithm and fails numerics. I’m probing padded output widths to see whether a smaller width selects the reference’s exact algorithm; I’ll only use a width that is exact for every batch class."}}
